2026-08-25T00:00:00Z (RFD66606-1021) 'A shared holographic algebra library
 # uuid: 6e120e09-ff41-537c-a78a-86bf8c54de3d
 # tags: rfd:title, rfd:attest-in:none
 RFD:Published  1 RFD
 Serials:Weftspun

2026-08-25T00:00:01Z (RFD66606-1021) '`weftspun_studio/`, `weftspun/elixir-holographic-reduced-representation`
 # tags: rfd:scope, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD1021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:02Z (RFD66606-1021) 'The studio core takes one shared holographic algebra library as a Git dependency.
 # tags: rfd:hook
 Text:RFD1021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:03Z (RFD66606-1021) 'Two representations of one idea is one too many. The two also do not interoperate, because a vector from one carries no meaning in the other.
 # tags: rfd:intrigue
 Text:RFD1021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:04Z (RFD66606-1021) 'Run the golden fixture `test/fixtures/hrr_golden.json` and check parity with the Python `holographic.py` reference to 1.0e-12. The sections below hold the rationale and the risks.
 # tags: rfd:exit
 Text:RFD1021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:05Z (RFD66606-1021) 'A shared holographic algebra library
 # tags: rfd:details-title, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD1021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:06Z (RFD66606-1021) '### Why the phase representation wins
 # tags: rfd:details-preamble
 Text:RFD1021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:07Z (RFD66606-1021) '| Point  | Phase representation                      | The earlier local module               |
 # tags: rfd:details-preamble
 Text:RFD1021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:08Z (RFD66606-1021) '| ------ | ----------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------- |
 # tags: rfd:details-preamble
 Text:RFD1021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:09Z (RFD66606-1021) '| Bind   | Adds phases. Cost is linear.              | Multiplies spectra. Cost is `n log n`. |
 # tags: rfd:details-preamble
 Text:RFD1021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:10Z (RFD66606-1021) '| Unbind | Subtracts phases. Exact for every vector. | Exact only after a unitary correction. |
 # tags: rfd:details-preamble
 Text:RFD1021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:11Z (RFD66606-1021) '| Atoms  | SHA-256 counter blocks.                   | A seeded normal draw.                  |
 # tags: rfd:details-preamble
 Text:RFD1021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:12Z (RFD66606-1021) '| Parity | Matches a Python reference bit for bit.   | None.                                  |
 # tags: rfd:details-preamble
 Text:RFD1021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:13Z (RFD66606-1021) '| Reuse  | Two repositories share it.                | One module in one repository.          |
 # tags: rfd:details-preamble
 Text:RFD1021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:14Z (RFD66606-1021) 'The phase form is cheaper, it is exact without a correction step, and a second language can produce the same vectors.
 # tags: rfd:details-preamble
 Text:RFD1021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:15Z (RFD66606-1021) '### What the library holds
 # tags: rfd:details-preamble
 Text:RFD1021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:16Z (RFD66606-1021) '`HRR` holds `encode_atom/2`, `bind/2`, `unbind/2`, `bundle/1`, `similarity/2`, `encode_text/2`, `to_binary/1`, `from_binary/1`, and `snr_estimate/2`.
 # tags: rfd:details-preamble
 Text:RFD1021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:17Z (RFD66606-1021) '`HRR.Cleanup` is new. It holds the codebook and the nearest-symbol lookup. Every caller of `unbind/2` needs that step, because an unbind returns the filler plus superposition noise. Writing it once stops three repositories from writing it again.
 # tags: rfd:details-preamble
 Text:RFD1021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:18Z (RFD66606-1021) '### What stays here
 # tags: rfd:details-preamble
 Text:RFD1021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:19Z (RFD66606-1021) '`WeftspunStudio.FactVector` holds the part that knows what a catalog fact is:
 # tags: rfd:details-preamble
 Text:RFD1021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:20Z (RFD66606-1021) '- `encode/2` binds the id, the category, and the tags to their roles, then bundles the result.
 # tags: rfd:details-preamble
 Text:RFD1021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:21Z (RFD66606-1021) '- `query/2` turns free text into a probe. A term may name any of the three roles, so the probe binds it to all three.
 # tags: rfd:details-preamble
 Text:RFD1021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:22Z (RFD66606-1021) '- `codebook/2` and `probe/4` reach `HRR.Cleanup` with the symbols a fact can resolve to.
 # tags: rfd:details-preamble
 Text:RFD1021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:23Z (RFD66606-1021) 'The library knows nothing about catalogs. This module knows nothing about phase arithmetic.
 # tags: rfd:details-preamble
 Text:RFD1021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:24Z (RFD66606-1021) 'Extract the earlier port into a library, and depend on it.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD1021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:25Z (RFD66606-1021) 'The library is `weftspun/elixir-holographic-reduced-representation`, which supplies the `:hrr` application and the `HRR` module. The studio core takes it as a Git dependency.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD1021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:26Z (RFD66606-1021) 'The algebra and the atom generation move over unchanged, so `test/fixtures/hrr_golden.json` still certifies parity with the Python `holographic.py` reference to 1.0e-12.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD1021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:27Z (RFD66606-1021) 'Dimension
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD1021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:28Z (RFD66606-1021) 'The library defaults to 4096. This project uses 1024.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:29Z (RFD66606-1021) 'A phase vector holds float64 values, so 4096 would take 32 kilobytes a row. At 1024 a row takes 8 kilobytes. A fact bundles four parts, and the capacity at 1024 is about 32 items, so the smaller width still leaves a wide margin.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:30Z (RFD66606-1021) 'Effects
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD1021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:31Z (RFD66606-1021) 'The stored vectors changed from 1024 float32 values to 1024 float64 phase angles. Migration `20260804010000` rewrites every row. Trust scores survive, because the vector comes from the other columns and never from itself.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:32Z (RFD66606-1021) '`mix ecto.migrate` starts the repository alone, so EXLA is not running. The migration therefore selects `Nx.BinaryBackend`. Phase encoding uses hashing and arithmetic, so it needs no accelerator.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:33Z (RFD66606-1021) 'Retrieval quality held. A search for `uv_unwrapping` returns `xatlas_uv_unwrapping` at 0.21, and the next result scores 0.015. A probe of the `:category` role of `trellis_text_to_textured_mesh` returns `text_to_textured_mesh` at 0.52.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:34Z (RFD66606-1021) 'Risks
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD1021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:35Z (RFD66606-1021) 'The library is a Git dependency, not a Hex package. A build therefore needs network access to GitHub. Publishing to Hex is a later step.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:36Z (RFD66606-1021) 'The library stores radians, not turns. A radian phase is irrational, so the exactness result does not reach it. The measured cost is 2.2e-15, which is 2.3e-11 of one grid step, and similarity after a round trip reads 1.0. Turns would remove the gap and break the golden fixture, so the library keeps radians.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:37Z (RFD66606-1021) 'Proofs
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD1021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:38Z (RFD66606-1021) 'The earlier repository proved the algebra in Lean 4, then deleted the proofs in commit 7303244 once the HRR code left it. The algebra now has a home again, so the proofs moved with it, into `formal/` of the library.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:39Z (RFD66606-1021) '`unbind_bind` and `bind_comm` transfer unchanged. `bind_assoc`, `unbind_bind_left`, and the two grid bounds are new. Together they say that binding is a commutative and associative group operation on `ℤ/65536`, and that unbinding inverts it exactly.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:40Z (RFD66606-1021) 'The cleanup recall walk from the same file did not move. It modelled `Recommender.Memory.recommend`, which no longer exists, and it needed `fire/plausible-witness-dag`. The restored model needs no dependency, and no axiom beyond `propext` and `Quot.sound`.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:41Z (RFD66606-1021) '`PhaseRat.lean` is new. It carries the grid result across to the arithmetic that runs it. A phase is a rational with a power-of-two denominator, so component `k` stands for `k / 2^16` of a turn. Binary64 holds a value exactly while its significand stays under `2^53`. Binding adds two numerators below `2^p`, so the exact sum needs `p + 1` bits, and `p = 16` leaves 36 bits spare. The addition and the subtraction therefore never round.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:42Z (RFD66606-1021) 'Three bridge theorems tie that file to `HrrModel`, so the bounds apply to the proved algebra and not to a lookalike.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:43Z (RFD66606-1021) 'Lean's `Float` is opaque and carries no formal semantics, so no proof mentions it. The theorems bound the significand, and the standard binary64 criterion does the rest.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:44Z (RFD66606-1021) 'Status
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
